# drag-hand: the pointer drags cards in your hand back and forth for 20 seconds while a
# recording plays, each drag a press, eight moves 16 ms apart and a release, and each drop
# inside the hand so that nothing is played. A bug report of lag while dragging hand cards
# came from the desktop app under the fleet's normal load. Written for a 1600 by 900 window,
# where the hand spans x 412 to 1190 at y 736 to 960 in verbs-zones.
#
# The frame log's summary counts the frames drawn while the button was held and how many of
# them were late (`dragging`). Run it under the machine's load as it is, and with busy
# threads added, and compare the late share during drags with the share over the run:
#
# just client app --drive drag-hand --fixture verbs-zones --for 22s
# just client app --drive drag-hand --fixture verbs-zones --for 22s --load 18
#
# A run with no window measures everything up to presentation. Whether a frame missed the
# display time its tick was for (`missed_target`) needs the desktop window's display link.
step 1500ms
drag 440,850 to 1160,780
step 60ms
drag 1160,780 to 440,850
step 60ms
drag 600,900 to 1000,760
step 60ms
drag 1000,760 to 600,900
step 60ms
drag 440,850 to 1160,780
step 60ms
drag 1160,780 to 440,850
step 60ms
drag 600,900 to 1000,760
step 60ms
drag 1000,760 to 600,900
step 60ms
drag 440,850 to 1160,780
step 60ms
